WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:07.510
Speaker 1: 206 marines have been discharged
for refusing the COVID vaccine.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:14.200
Now you might say a away, but David, don't
they get the hep a vaccine and the happy vaccine

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:20.750
and the flu vaccine and the MMR vaccine and
the meningococcal vaccine and the polio virus

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.520
vaccine and the tetanus diphtheria vaccine
and the varicella vaccine?

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.480
And depending on where they're deployed, the
anthrax vaccine and the Haemophilus influenza

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.270
type B vaccine and the Japanese encephalitis
vaccine and the pneumococcal vaccine and the

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.489
rabies, smallpox, typhoid, yellow fever.

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:40.489
OK.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:41.489
All right.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:42.719
Yes, they do.

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:44.760
But this is different.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.120
This is about their rights.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.230
All right.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:53.140
So the bottom line is every time we hear they're
going to lose a third of the service.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:01:00.840
NYPD one third are saying 34 New York Police
Department officers actually discharged, actually

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.840
discharged.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:10.060
And so when I read more than 200 marines removed
for defying COVID mandate, I think this seems

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.969
like a good thing.

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:18.710
What I mean by that is when we found out at
the end of the day, 34 NYPD officers were

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.170
removed for not getting the vaccine.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:27.899
I don't know that those are the good apples
that we actually want in NYPD anyway.

00:01:27.899 --> 00:01:34.210
And much the same way, if these are the two
hundred and six that are being removed, there's

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.359
something like 18000 marines or something.

00:01:37.359 --> 00:01:39.609
No, I'm sorry, 180000 Marines.

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:43.079
This represents 0.11 percent of them.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:44.409
I think this is fine.

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:46.499
These don't sound like team player.

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:50.709
Marines report from Axios U.S. Marine Corps
said it removed two hundred and six service

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.849
members for refusing the vaccine.

00:01:52.849 --> 00:01:57.170
Updated numbers come as DOD has ramped up
repercussions for those defying the vaccine

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.170
order.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.649
The branch said it had already discharged
103.

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:06.270
The big picture Approximately 94 percent of
active members are fully vaccinated.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:11.441
As of last week, roughly 98 percent of all
active duty forces, including reserves, have

00:02:11.441 --> 00:02:13.230
received the vaccine.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:18.329
Remember that Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin
in August said all troops must get the vaccine,

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:20.969
encouraged service leaders to set up their
own timelines.

00:02:20.969 --> 00:02:27.640
To date, approximately 3847 requests for religious
accommodation over the vaccine have been made.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.890
Zero have been approved, according to a Marine
Corps communication officer.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.780
One note about that.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.989
This doesn't mean everyone else is vaccinated.

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:45.469
Some of those requests, although they haven't
been approved for an exemption, they may still

00:02:45.469 --> 00:02:46.700
be in process.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.030
So that's where you get.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.500
That's why we're still short of 100 percent.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.939
There are people who have made a request for
an exemption.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:58.989
It has not yet been adjudicated or even if
it has, it has not yet led to a discharge.

00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:02.549
And so that's all going to have to sort of
be be sorted out.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:11.540
Service members can request to opt out of
mandatory health elements on the base of vaccination

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:16.560
on the basis of a health situation, an administrative
reason.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.420
I don't know exactly what would count as that
or a religious exemption.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:24.770
Those can be temporarily granted or permanently
granted.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:29.120
So far from what we're seeing, none of them
have been granted for marines.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.319
I read a comment and I don't I don't know.

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:36.370
I mean, this is it's just a comment from one
member of the U.S. Navy that there are service

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:43.109
members who are looking for a way out and
that refusing a vaccine is a way to get an

00:03:43.109 --> 00:03:44.860
honorable discharge.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.459
Maybe benefits, maybe benefits.

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:53.310
Although we're hearing conflicting things
about benefits and that this is a way for

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.540
some people who are looking to leave anyway
to do it while saving face.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:03.670
That's one opinion from one member of the
U.S. Navy who wrote to me.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.670
Take it for what it is, which is which is
simply an anecdote.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:14.659
But the the big takeaway continues to be the
legality of these requirements is not in question.

00:04:14.659 --> 00:04:17.599
The morality can be argued.

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:20.699
The effectiveness is also not in question.

00:04:20.699 --> 00:04:26.110
These work and, you know, United Airlines
was a big one where much hubbub was made and

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:30.030
like everybody got vaccinated other than I
think it was 200 people or something like

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.030
that.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.400
So these requirements do work.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.509
There's a fair debate to be had about in the
context of Comic-Con, where there is only

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:43.610
some protection, some protection from two
doses against getting an asymptomatic infection.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.360
What is really the goal here?

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.580
Well, the primary goal seems to be to keep
the burden on hospitals down by preventing

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.479
people from ending up hospitalized.

00:04:52.479 --> 00:04:54.620
But these next four weeks are going to be
wild.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.970
The numbers are insane that we are seeing,
and maybe by tomorrow, maybe by Wednesday,

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:03.600
we'll have kind of like the full catch caught
up numbers from the holiday and then we'll

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:04.150
see how things are looking at that point.

